# Cloudflare Workers static-asset response headers.
# Copied verbatim to dist/ by Vite; read by Cloudflare, never served to visitors.
#
# WHY `no-transform` ON HTML (FOUNDATIONS §6):
# Cloudflare Web Analytics injects <script src="static.cloudflareinsights.com/
# beacon.min.js"> into HTML responses AT THE EDGE — not from our build. Our CSP
# blocks it, so no data ever leaves, but it is still a third-party script request
# on every load and a console error, against the spirit of §6.
#
# The dashboard toggle that disables it (account -> Web Analytics -> Manage site
# -> Disable) lives outside this repo: invisible to review, silently reversible,
# and gone entirely if the site is ever moved to a new zone or account. This is
# the in-repo half of the fix. Cloudflare cannot inject into a response it is not
# permitted to transform, so `no-transform` blocks the rewrite at the protocol
# level, wherever this artifact is hosted.
#
# HTML ONLY, deliberately. `no-transform` also forbids re-encoding, so applying
# it to /assets/* would cost gzip/brotli on the 259 KB bundle (90 KB gzipped).
# The beacon is only ever injected into HTML, so that is all we need to cover.
#
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` matches what Cloudflare already served for these
# routes — this adds `no-transform` without changing caching behavior.
#
# Verify after deploy (the injection is user-agent gated, so a plain curl will
# NOT see it and DevTools is the awkward way to check):
#   npm run deploy   # its beacon gate does exactly this check, and fails on a hit

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform

# /methods.html 307-redirects here; this is the route that actually serves.
/methods
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform

/methods.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
